= Same-graph ordinary U versus soft H: source audit

This is a historical run report. Its findings and summary measurements are retained; raw logs, JSON receipts, and JUnit reports are not distributed with the source. Historical artifact names and local paths below identify the original run, not files available in this checkout.
<same-graph-ordinary-u-versus-soft-h-source-audit>
The 314 GiB failure is not explained merely by saying that a soft operator has more terms. The current direct implementation has #strong[no U/S/US forest-node triplication or residue-key Cartesian product] at the inspected boundaries. It already forms `H(X) = S(X) + U(X - S(X))`. The concrete soft-specific growth opportunity is inside each completed branch: S constructs a Taylor coefficient and U then processes the larger, potentially only partially cancelled remainder. That is a candidate boundary, not a measured cause of the large failure.

This audit is read-only. No generation, rerun, source changes, graph-numerator expansion, or new profile was performed. The bounds-panic diagnosis explains the final crash mechanism hypothesis; it does not explain why the expression grew.

== Shared inputs and first differences
<shared-inputs-and-first-differences>
For the #strong[same imported graph, model, canonical LMB, cuts, selected production keys, retained UV regions and disabled integrated terms];, change the two existing positive-degree `IR` prescriptions to `MUV`. Both prescriptions retain the same classified regions: classification removes `Unsubtracted`, while `Spinney::with_scheme` chooses its LMB independently of the scheme. The wood deduplicates by subgraph filter, and operation identity is the canonical trace key. Thus an IR→MUV-only change should preserve the wood/forest topology, apart from labels identifying the scheme. Sources: #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/uv_graph.rs:156")[classification];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/spinney.rs:87")[scheme-independent LMB];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/hedge_poset.rs:207")[wood filter deduplication];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/hedge_poset.rs:420")[operation identity];.

A control must change the actual `renormalization_prescription` rules. The legacy `uv.softct` field is declared/defaulted but has no production read in the repository-wide Rust search; production dispatch reads the chosen scheme. `subtract_uv=false` removes the forest and therefore cannot isolate soft H from ordinary U. Sources: #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/settings.rs:201")[prescription selection];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/settings.rs:459")[softct field];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/uv_graph.rs:174")[bare classification];.

Ordered direct pipeline: stored parent CFF and exact production key → component-owned numerator mapping → common `start` momentum/OSE setup → #strong[first operator difference: U versus S followed by U on X−S(X)] → same branch-owned cograph numerator mapping/normalization → materialize key selectors or replace them by one → sum forest-node final atoms → evaluator preprocessing. #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/approx/direct_3d/kernel.rs:338")[Kernel dispatch];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/approx/direct_3d/kernel.rs:375")[H remainder form already implemented];, #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/approx/final_integrand.rs:117")[final direct assembly];.

Ordinary U performs one projection; positive-degree H performs two. Logarithmic IR (`dod==0`) directly takes the ordinary U path. There is no general constant size multiplier: nesting feeds a completed child atom into the next operation, and Taylor coefficients can increase internal algebra substantially even when the number of typed sectors/keys is unchanged. The implementation does not explicitly call `expand` on graph numerators in this direct pipeline. The `series(...).to_atom()` boundary still materializes coefficient algebra; absence of an explicit `expand` call is not a bound on its size. #link("../../../crates/gammalooprs/src/uv/approx/direct_3d/kernel.rs:719")[Projection and series];.

